  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pop Council, SGBV phase III, 2014-2017 - Population Council Gender Based Violence</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Pop Council, k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld fas III, 2014-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To mitigate the consequences and occurrence of SGBV by strengthening the capacities of the medical, legal and justice sectors to care for survivors of such violence.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Population Council (the council) arbetar med att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra medicinska och juridiska sektorers capacitet att bem&#xf6;ta &#xf6;verlevare av sexuellt och k&#xf6;nsrelaterad v&#xe5;ld (SGBV). The council har under de senaste sju &#xe5;ren, med st&#xf6;d av Svenska Ambassaden i Lusaka, arbetat med att bygga upp en faktabas kring SGBV, anpassad f&#xf6;r s&#xf6;dra och &#xf6;stra Afrika. Under f&#xf6;reg&#xe5;ende projektfas identifierade the council samt partners behovet att bygga kompetens kring barn och flyktingkvinnor som drabbats av k&#xf6;nsrelaterat v&#xe5;ld. B&#xe5;da dessa grupper bed&#xf6;ms vara extra s&#xe5;rbara f&#xf6;r att drabbas av SGBV och ha s&#xe4;rskilda v&#xe5;rdbehov efter de varit utsatta f&#xf6;r &#xf6;vergrepp som skiljer sig fr&#xe5;n kvinnor i den generella befolkningen. 

The council vill d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r, tillsammans med partners, dels genomf&#xf6;ra studier som kartl&#xe4;gger f&#xf6;rekomsten av SGBV mot barn och flyktingkvinnor och dels genomf&#xf6;ra studier som provar metoder f&#xf6;r hur existerande insatser f&#xf6;r &#xf6;verlevare av SGBV kan anpassas till barn och flyktingkvinnor. 

The council vill &#xe4;ven forts&#xe4;tta med det arbete organisationen gjort kring integrering av insatser f&#xf6;r s&#xe4;kra aborter i generellt bem&#xf6;tande av &#xf6;verlevare av SGBV. 

Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att dessa delar sammantaget ska leda till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade policies och program f&#xf6;r &#xf6;verlevare av SGBV i s&#xf6;dra och &#xf6;stra Afrika.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World-wide, 35% of all women have experienced either sexual and/or physical intimate partner violence or non-partner sexual violence. Consequences of sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV) could be stigmatisation, discrimination, physical and psychical suffering and transmission of infectious diseases, among them HIV. 

The project proposal submitted by Population Council (hereafter the council) focuses on three key populations of SGBV survivors in East and Southern Africa: women in the general population, female refugees and children. The overall objective of the proposed project is to mitigate the consequences and occurrence of SGBV by strengthening the capacities of the medical, legal and justice sectors to care for survivors of such voilence.  

Many of the survivors of SGBV are children and there is a lack of knowledge on suitable approaches for targeting children. Refugee women are increasingly vulnerable to SGBV, due to the particular setting that they live in, lacking the safety of a home. Through replicating the already tested SGBV responses to target children and refugees, the council intends to strenghen the evidence-base on occurance of SGBV and methods for reaching survivors of SGBV that are refugees or children. By strengthen the evidence-base, the council expect to influence regional policy and programs on SGBV to better meet the needs of survivors, through dissemination of results to key audiences.</narrative>
  </description>
